    "pdm_lifestyle_tips_bCbTKb": {
      "type": "pdm_lifestyle-tips",
      "blocks": {
        "tip_qdCXLz": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Be mindful of what you eat",
            "description": "<p>Your diet can influence your skin. Processed foods and seed oils like sunflower or soybean oil can increase inflammation, which may worsen acne. Instead, try incorporating omega-3-rich foods like salmon and walnuts to help keep your skin calm and clear.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/d386ec15d10c5755f14d57eb778dc9c1.jpg",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_8x8iED": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Keep your beauty tools clean",
            "description": "<p>Makeup brushes, sponges, and even your phone can gather bacteria that lead to clogged pores. Regularly cleaning these tools can reduce the chances of breakouts and help keep your skin fresh.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/247d6ff249e6b578cb132da9de64c714.jpg",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_WqzmXT": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Switch up your pillowcase",
            "description": "<p>Consider using a pillowcase with copper oxide. These have been shown to help prevent and heal acne due to copper’s antimicrobial properties. And make sure to wash or change your pillowcase every 2-3 days, as it can collect sweat, oil, and dead skin cells, which may lead to breakouts.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/b826c4de38f155618b4d351325d8d365.jpg",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_ChLfdj": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Skip the fabric softeners",
            "description": "<p>Fabric softeners might make your laundry feel nice, but they can leave a waxy residue on pillowcases and towels, which can clog your pores and cause acne. Stick to plain detergent for anything that touches your face.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/image_2_cb9d5733-49d9-4146-a93b-d9d106b5934e.png",
            "sources": ""
          }
        },
        "tip_mRnVgk": {
          "type": "tip",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Cleanse and exfoliate regularly",
            "description": "<p>Daily cleansing helps remove bacteria, makeup, and pore-clogging buildup. Use a gentle cleanser that won’t strip your skin’s natural oils, and avoid products with alcohol. Exfoliate once a week with a peel containing salicylic acid, a Beta Hydroxy Acid (BHA), which gets deep into your pores to clear out dead skin cells. This helps prevent blackheads, pimples, and irritation.</p>",
            "image_card": "shopify://shop_images/785c293f90cef7428f41807ece9718a4.jpg",
            "sources": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "tip_qdCXLz",
        "tip_8x8iED",
        "tip_WqzmXT",
        "tip_ChLfdj",
        "tip_mRnVgk"
      ],
